<title>UK: Johnson Matthey shares up after &quot;buy&quot; note.</title>
<headline>Johnson Matthey shares up after &quot;buy&quot; note.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Johnson Matthey Plc climbed on Wednesday as analysts at SBC Warburg shaved their profit forecasts for the metals and industrial materials group but restated a &quot;buy&quot; recommendation on the stock, dealers said.</p>
<p>The shares were up nine pence at 582-1/2 by 1023 GMT.</p>
<p>Analysts at SBC Warburg were not immediately available for comment but market sources confirmed they had restated their recommendation on the stock despite a cut in profit forecasts for 1997 and 1998.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
